(1,'KEEP',[I],'experimental','Rolling inertia as a measurement of a supplied mass-scaling exponent','The statement operationally defines m(r)=k*r^D and gives rolling speed/height measurements. Rotational energy and radial mass integration infer D under the stated averaged spherical model. Fractal terminology introduces no external physical law.'),
