(7,'BORDERLINE',[I,II],'theory','Satellite-droplet ring produced by impact on a table','The actual photo shows the central drop and separate satellite ring. Momentum and surface energy support scaling, but crown breakup, droplet launch and impact/wetting assumptions are not supplied. The intended mechanism and necessary model remain genuinely ambiguous.'),
(8,'KEEP',[I,III],'theory','Stationary capillary bubble in centrifugal hydrostatic pressure','Slow spin-up and stationary final shape avoid an unsupplied fluid transient. Rotating-frame hydrostatics, gas pressure-volume balance and surface-tension force balance determine the interface and size. Nonlinear curvature geometry is mathematics.'),
(9,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Skipping-stone dynamics with an explicitly supplied hydrodynamic force','The rendered immersed-area, normal and tangent geometry and full lift/friction force are supplied. Newtonian impulse, energy and repeated-flight dynamics suffice without importing a specialized water-impact law.'),
(10,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Rain-induced car power losses from momentum and energy transfer','Additional rain interception, acceleration of collected water and water displacement losses can be estimated using mass flux, momentum and mechanical work. Empirical numerical parameters are inputs, not new required physics.'),
(11,'KEEP',[III,IV],'numerical','Air-well condensation estimates from heat and water-vapour budgets','The task asks realistic estimates rather than an exact transport solution. Vapour saturation, latent heat, airflow/diffusive supply and cooling energy set yields and interaction scales. Ordinary gas kinetic/thermal reasoning permits explicit approximation choices; climate/geometry inputs are not specified.'),
(12,'KEEP',[IV],'theory','Different mechanical behaviour of glacier and frozen sea ice','Salt rejection and trapped brine/porosity during ordinary freezing explain the qualitative contrast. No quantitative fracture or specialized crystal constitutive law is requested.'),
(13,'KEEP',[III,IV],'theory','Condensation versus deposition when cooling argon and carbon dioxide','Ordinary phase-path reasoning explains flowing condensed argon collecting before freezing, versus carbon-dioxide deposition along the cold tube. The different melting/phase properties are material data, not a new specialized theory.'),
(14,'KEEP',[IV],'theory','Maximum heating of one of three isolated finite heat reservoirs','First-law energy conservation and entropy/Carnot constraints for constant heat capacities decide the attainable temperature. Engines and refrigerators introduce ordinary thermodynamics only.'),
(15,'REJECT',[IV],'theory','Constructing mixture free energy from a closed miscibility gap','The rendered concentration-temperature ellipse is supplied, but chemical-potential equality and the common-tangent phase-separation construction are not. These specialized binary-mixture thermodynamic rules are central to the sole free-energy reconstruction task.'),
(16,'REJECT',[],'theory','Defect-free semiconductor epitaxial-film critical thickness','Crystal lattice mismatch, strain/dislocation energy and the critical-thickness model are unsupplied. They determine the entire silicon-on-GaAs thickness bound; ordinary energy conservation cannot specify their constitutive relations.'),
(17,'KEEP',[X],'theory','Finite-aperture lens image of an extended nearby cylinder','Lens power, aperture, eye distance and cork dimensions fully specify paraxial ray construction and visibility. The requested scaled drawing is conventional geometric optics.'),
(18,'KEEP',[X],'numerical','Ray envelopes of sunlight reflected from a sinusoidal water surface','The stationary sinusoidal reflecting geometry and illumination direction are supplied. Reflection and envelope differentiation locate caustics, singularities and parameter dependence without a fluid-wave model.'),
(19,'KEEP',[VI,X],'theory','Electrostatic wedge capacitor with supplied anisotropic dielectric axes','The render defines the wedge and principal axes. A linear permittivity tensor is specified; electrostatic potential, D divergence and dielectric energy define the field problem. Coordinate rescaling and field-line integration are mathematics.'),
(20,'KEEP',[I,VI],'theory','Charged and neutral metal-sphere elastic collision','Conducting-sphere induction, charge redistribution at contact, energy and momentum determine the separated velocities under the printed ideal elastic assumption. No advanced microscopic metal model is required.'),
(21,'KEEP',[VI],'theory','Optimizing a surface dipole field under a fixed-area constraint','The dipole direction at every surface point is explicitly defined. Ordinary electrostatic dipole superposition and geometric optimization determine the field, including possible lack of a finite optimum without a distance constraint.'),
