(26,'KEEP',[],'theory','Domain error in a supplied differential-operator square','The wavefunction, differential Hamiltonian and two conflicting expectation expressions are explicit. Normalization and operator boundary-domain analysis resolve the apparent contradiction: the first derivative application leaves the hard-wall operator domain. No unsupplied quantum dynamical or measurement law is needed.'),
(27,'BORDERLINE',[XI],'theory','Angle-angular-momentum uncertainty on a periodic quantum domain','Angular-momentum quantization is within the stated light/atomic scope, but the periodic angle operator and modified uncertainty/domain rule are not supplied. Whether elementary quantization plus periodic probability suffices for the intended explanation is unresolved.'),
(28,'REJECT',[],'theory','Exact oscillator-two-level quantum time evolution beyond rotating-wave approximation','The Hamiltonian is supplied, but ladder-operator action, quantum oscillator/coherent states and unitary time-evolution rules are not. These central prerequisites cannot be replaced by ordinary finite-matrix algebra.'),
(29,'BORDERLINE',[X,IX],'theory','Pulse group velocity in a pumped two-line gas','The two-transition diagram, linewidth limit and classical-oscillator permission support ordinary dispersion. However pumping-to-population/oscillator-strength and gain parameters are not operationally specified, leaving ambiguity over the central two-line susceptibility model and numerical group velocity.'),
(30,'BORDERLINE',[],'theory','Short-time purity constraint under a supplied quantum master equation','The full evolution equation, variance, purity bounds and thermal length are supplied. Much work is trace algebra, but the canonical position-momentum commutator needed for the friction contribution is not stated. Supplied-model sufficiency remains uncertain rather than treating the quantum label alone as rejection.'),
(31,'REJECT',[],'theory','Covariant weight of a charged orbiting particle in Schwarzschild gravity','Some background field tensors are supplied, but the metric, covariant particle equation/geodesic connection and gravitational force interpretation are not. These central GR prerequisites are necessary for support and covariant weight.'),
